    "markdown": "## Baseline capabilities\n\nAudistill 0.4.0 is the first release line with the core local-first workflow in place.\n\n### Local-first Episode Library\n\n- Create Episodes from local audio files, YouTube links, RSS feed items, and direct media URLs.\n- Keep completed Episodes self-contained with Transcript, Tabs, Source provenance, and Chat history stored locally.\n- Organize the Library with Inbox, folders, nested folders, Starred Episodes, search, sorting, drag-and-drop, and bulk actions.\n\n### On-device Transcription\n\n- Download and manage the local Transcription Model.\n- Run Transcription on-device, with progress states for queued, downloading, transcribing, generating, complete, cancelled, and error Episodes.\n- Retry failed or cancelled work without losing existing Library data.\n\n### Recipes, Tabs, and Chat\n\n- Use built-in Recipes to generate Brief, Detailed, and Full Tabs from Transcripts.\n- Create, duplicate, edit, and delete custom Recipes, including per-Recipe Model overrides.\n- Pick a Pipeline Recipe that runs during Ingest.\n- Edit, regenerate, copy, and export Tab content with rich Markdown rendering, including tables, highlights, task lists, and Mermaid diagrams.\n- Use per-Episode Chat with Library-aware tools and Tab-writing actions.\n\n### BYOK Models and licensing\n\n- Connect your own OpenRouter API key and choose the Model used for Recipe execution and Chat.\n- Use the 14-day Trial in official builds, then activate a one-time License through Polar.\n- Keep existing Episodes viewable even when creation features are gated.\n\n### macOS app experience\n\n- Signed macOS builds support automatic update checks, downloaded update banners, restart-to-install, and update dismissal.\n- The app restores window state and open workspace tabs across restarts."
